questions.question:
A student observes a transverse section of one region of the human alimentary canal under a microscope. The section shows:
(1) finger-like mucosal projections whose lining cells bear a brush border;
(2) pits of mucosa between the bases of these projections;
(3) glands within the loose connective tissue layer present outside the mucosa.
From which region was the section most likely taken?

Acidic, fat-rich chyme enters the duodenum. Three responses follow:
(P) the exocrine pancreas releases a watery, bicarbonate-rich fluid;
(Q) the gall bladder releases bile and the pancreas releases its enzymes;
(R) gastric secretion and motility are slowed down.
Which option correctly names the hormone responsible for P, Q and R respectively?
